I fixed #1201 and committed it as 2c0f2bc9. /grep and yoyo grep now read every word after the pattern as a path, never as a git branch, tag or HEAD. Format, clippy and the full cargo test all pass.

The fix: all three git-grep builders (run_grep_in, run_grep_count_in, run_grep_with_context_in) now send -e <pattern> -- <paths>. That is the same shape yoagent's own search tool uses. Before, the -- sat in front of the pattern, so it only stopped option parsing and git still read the following words as revisions.

Tests: a new file, src/commands_search_grep_rev_tests.rs, builds a real git repo in a temp dir. Each case runs through all three builders. Four cases failed on the old code:
• a dir named main while branch main exists: git refused with "ambiguous argument";
• a dir v1/ plus tag v1: the same refusal;
• dev + src/main.rs, where dev is a branch but not a path: an empty result, which is why this repo printed "No matches found";
• HEAD with no such file: the count builder searched the HEAD commit instead of a path.

These stayed green: a plain src/ path, a pattern starting with - (-foo), and no path at all.

One change beyond the plan: with the new argument order, git grep says nothing about a path that doesn't exist, so a mistyped path would have silently turned into "No matches". The shared grep_output_parts in src/grep_status.rs now names each missing path (git repos only; globs and :(...) pathspecs are left to git). It shows that error alongside the other paths' matches and exits 2, which is what plain grep already does.

An existing test, missing_path_in_the_git_arm_is_gits_own_fatal, expected git's exit 128 with no matches. That error only happened because git was treating the missing word as a revision, which is this bug. I renamed it to ..._is_named_beside_the_matches, changed its assertions to the new behaviour, and noted in its comment that the old claim no longer holds.

On the built binary in this repo: yoyo grep fn main src/main.rs now lists the fn matches in src/main.rs and reports main: no such file or directory, exit 2. The plan expected exit 0, but in this repo main is a branch and not a path, so exit 2 is correct. Plain grep -rnH -- fn main m.rs outside git prints the same thing and also exits 2.

Also checked or changed:
• Non-git fallback: it was already correct (cmd.arg("--").arg(&args.pattern), around line 1573), so I left it alone.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md said git grep "refuses the whole search" when a path is missing. That is no longer true, so I rewrote it.
• Module size: commands_search.rs was already at 4780 lines against its recorded limit of 4778. The fix adds no production lines there; the 4 new lines are the test module declaration. I re-recorded the limit at 4784 in tests/module_size.rs.
• Git gate: the git_chokepoint check caught my first version calling git directly. The test setup now goes through run_git_in_dir, like the neighbouring tests.
